   "text": "I read the structure as a cyclic octadepsipeptide, a PF1022A-type ring with two morpholinophenyl groups, and wrote the SMILES from the ring order and the wedge/hash bonds.\n\n**Ring sequence.** Going around the macrocycle, the eight residues alternate between amide-linked and ester-linked units:\nN-Me-Leu \u2013 lactate \u2013 N-Me-Leu \u2013 4-morpholinophenyl-lactate \u2013 N-Me-Leu \u2013 lactate \u2013 N-Me-Leu \u2013 4-morpholinophenyl-lactate.\nEach N-Me-Leu carries an isobutyl side chain and an N-methyl on the ring nitrogen. Each phenyllactate carries a CH2 linked to a para-substituted benzene bearing a morpholine nitrogen.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** I assigned each centre from the drawn wedges and hashes using CIP priorities:\n- The N-methyl-leucine \u03b1-carbons are S (L-Leu); I checked the top-left one from its wedge, and the other three are drawn the same way.\n- The lactate \u03b1-carbons are R (D-lactate), from the hashed methyl.\n- The phenyllactate \u03b1-carbons are R (D), from the hashed benzyl CH2.\n\nI assumed the symmetry-related residues share the stereochemistry of the ones I checked.\n\nSMILES: CN1[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)O[C@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)O[C@H](Cc2ccc(N3CCOCC3)cc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)O[C@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)O[C@H](Cc2ccc(N3CCOCC3)cc2)C1=O"
